ntains an ‘archaic’ text belonging to the the Σ-group and with a reduced number of paleae in the text, which were integrated partly at a later time. The codex was used in several schools in Italy and in Southern France. In the first layer of glosses is a copy of the Glossa ordinaria by Johannes Teutonicus (published in 1215/16), in the following layers there is a copy by several hands of Bartholomew of Brescia’s additiones to the Glossa ordinaria, as well as glosses by canonists mainly from the 13th and 14th centuries.</dc:description><dc:format>I + 227 ff., 36 x 27.5 cm</dc:format><dc:identifier>doi:10.5076/e-codices-acs-0089</dc:identifier><dc:identifier>http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/en/list/one/acs/0089</dc:identifier><dc:identifier>Sion/Sitten, Archives du Chapitre/Kapitelsarchiv, Ms. 89</dc:identifier><dc:publisher>e-codices - Virtual Manuscript Library of Switzerland</dc:publisher><dc:language>Latin</dc:language><dc:relation>Descrizione di Giovanna Murano, per e-codices, 2016.</dc:relation><dc:rights>e-codices / Sion/Sitten, Archives du Chapitre/Kapitelsarchiv (cf. http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/en/about/terms)</dc:rights><dc:source rdf:resource="http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/en/list/one/acs/0089"></dc:source><dc:title>Sion/Sitten, Archives du Chapitre/Kapitelsarchiv, Ms. 89 : Decretum Gratiani</dc:title><dc:type>Manuscript</dc:type><dcterms:medium>Parchment</dcterms:medium><edm:europeanaProxy>false</edm:europeanaProxy><ore:proxyFor rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/item/9200211/en_list_one_acs_0089"/><ore:proxyIn rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/aggregation/provider/9200211/en_list_one_acs_0089"/><edm:type>TEXT</edm:type></ore:Proxy><edm:EuropeanaAggregation rdf:about="http://data.europeana.eu/aggregation/europeana/9200211/en_list_one_acs_0089"><edm:aggregatedCHO rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/item/9200211/en_list_one_acs_0089"/><edm:datasetName>9200211_Ag_EU_e-Codices</edm:datasetName><edm:country>Switzerland</edm:country><edm:preview rdf:r